WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:02.110
In the present time,

00:02.580 --> 00:05.900
With VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.900 --> 00:08.970
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.910 --> 00:17.830
And there exists

00:17.830 --> 00:21.960
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:21.960 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the name of that game is...

00:26.890 --> 00:29.130
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:50.150 --> 00:56.120
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:10.400 --> 02:11.780
Fall to death.

02:12.230 --> 02:16.070
It kills anyone, NPCs,
players, and monsters.

02:16.070 --> 02:18.490
A death sentence by the physics engine.

02:21.800 --> 02:24.460
I call this "Scorpion Fall."

02:28.460 --> 02:32.790
Operation to mass kill Crystal Scorpions...
is a huge success!

02:33.970 --> 02:38.470
#30: AN IMPULSE CALLED HUNGER,
A TENACITY CALLED CRAVING

02:42.350 --> 02:46.400
All right.
I've killed that many Crystal Scorpions.

02:46.400 --> 02:49.980
I bet my level will skyrocket!

02:57.220 --> 02:58.590
Huh?

02:58.590 --> 03:02.840
It's weird. They should've already
hit the ground by now.

03:03.480 --> 03:06.000
Why am I not getting any EXP?

03:08.460 --> 03:11.210
EXP is awarded after the battle ended...

03:11.880 --> 03:14.630
If I haven't gotten any, that means...

03:15.630 --> 03:18.220
The battle is not over yet?

03:24.100 --> 03:26.640
I knew it. Some came swarming in.

03:26.640 --> 03:29.480
It's a hassle, but I'll just drop
you guys off the cliff again...

03:43.540 --> 03:44.580
Huh?

03:53.960 --> 03:58.300
A-A golden Crystal Scorpion?!

03:59.970 --> 04:01.850
Is it a Rare Enemy?

04:03.220 --> 04:06.980
RARE ENEMY
GOLDY SCORPION

04:07.400 --> 04:12.110
It's messing with the Crystal Scorpions
like they're toys or something...

04:20.780 --> 04:26.700
Looks like that golden one is not the type
to come in a pack like the regular ones.

04:28.120 --> 04:32.210
In that case, making it fall off
a cliff would be difficult.

04:32.210 --> 04:33.840
Then what do I do?

04:33.840 --> 04:34.840
Run?

04:34.840 --> 04:38.550
I can avoid this battle
if I hide in the Inventoria.

04:41.050 --> 04:41.720
But...

04:42.300 --> 04:45.560
As a gamer, running away...

04:46.350 --> 04:48.270
...is not an option!

04:48.770 --> 04:50.100
Fine.

04:50.100 --> 04:52.770
I'm a lone wolf right now too.

04:52.770 --> 04:54.730
I'll take you on, one-on-one!

04:54.730 --> 04:55.730
TRANSIENT - NITROGAIN
I'll take you on, one-on-one!

04:59.150 --> 05:01.070
It split it in two?!

05:02.820 --> 05:06.870
Its claws are sharpened,
making it more suitable for attack.

05:12.040 --> 05:14.710
It's completely different
from the regular type.

05:14.710 --> 05:18.050
It's better to think of it as having
two broadsword wielders for arms.

05:23.050 --> 05:26.310
The golden crystal is
covering its entire body...

05:26.310 --> 05:30.230
It doesn't feel as sturdy
as the regular ones,

05:30.230 --> 05:35.400
but going from titanium to plain steel
won't make my attacks work any better!

05:35.400 --> 05:37.320
I can't exactly call it a positive.

05:38.230 --> 05:39.110
Whoa!

05:44.410 --> 05:47.910
And not only that, in exchange,
it got a lot more speed!

05:48.620 --> 05:53.960
I get to fight it one-on-one thanks
to it killing the Crystal Scorpions,

05:53.960 --> 06:00.170
but I need to avoid leaving this area
the best I can to keep this battle compact.

06:00.170 --> 06:03.680
Against this golden scorpion...

06:04.070 --> 06:05.680
Heh, what an absurd challenge.

06:05.680 --> 06:07.140
I couldn't help but laugh.

06:15.480 --> 06:17.980
It even got a long-range attack!?

06:17.980 --> 06:20.480
And it's clearly poisonous!

06:20.480 --> 06:23.240
I'm starting to understand this guy.

06:23.700 --> 06:25.490
To sum it up...

06:26.780 --> 06:28.410
It's specialized in battle!

06:28.410 --> 06:33.910
It's got the offense, defense, speed,
and even both close and long-range attacks.

06:33.910 --> 06:35.170
But...

06:41.380 --> 06:43.630
Poison again? How obvious.

06:44.130 --> 06:47.550
I just have to focus on where its stinger
is pointing at, and it's avo—

06:51.770 --> 06:54.640
A barrage?! I...

06:54.640 --> 06:56.480
...can't dodge this!

07:04.990 --> 07:06.910
That was damn close!

07:06.910 --> 07:08.660
I barely teleported away in time!

07:08.660 --> 07:09.300
INVENTORIA - STORAGE SPACE

07:09.300 --> 07:11.080
INVENTORIA - STORAGE SPACE
That bastard can also spray

07:11.080 --> 07:14.160
INVENTORIA - STORAGE SPACE
its poison like a shotgun?!

07:14.660 --> 07:16.080
Calm down.

07:16.080 --> 07:19.390
Mental distress will affect
your avatar's movements.

07:19.920 --> 07:22.920
INVENTORIA
STORAGE SPACE

07:24.670 --> 07:27.300
Even if I use my MP recovery potions,

07:27.300 --> 07:31.470
I can only get into
Inventoria six or so times.

07:31.470 --> 07:34.430
Can't exactly use them willy-nilly.

07:36.350 --> 07:37.850
Exit Travel!

07:42.070 --> 07:44.650
Anyway, that poison barrage is bad news.

07:45.850 --> 07:51.160
It'll be hard to avoid at close range
unless I flee into Inventoria.

07:59.710 --> 08:01.160
But to put it in another way,

08:01.160 --> 08:04.170
if I can do something about its stinger,
I can seize the advantage!

08:05.170 --> 08:10.040
Plus, I'm starting to see my way out
with these repeated attacks.

08:11.090 --> 08:15.680
At first, I thought its golden scales
had no weak spots at all.

08:15.680 --> 08:21.110
But perhaps to allow for more mobility,
it's got tiny open spaces all over its body!

08:22.070 --> 08:23.690
Gotta fight poison with poison.

08:24.020 --> 08:24.940
WEAPON UNEQUIPPED

08:25.280 --> 08:26.190
EMPIRE BEE TWINBLADES
EQUIPPED

08:26.640 --> 08:28.360
Empire Bee Twinblades...

08:28.360 --> 08:29.950
The right blade has Corrosive Poison

08:29.950 --> 08:33.200
CORROSIVE POSION
that inflicts corrode attribute.

08:33.200 --> 08:35.660
Corrosive Poison will contaminate
the attacked spot

08:35.660 --> 08:37.790
and gradually corrode
the target from the inside.

08:37.790 --> 08:38.960
Glowing Pierce!

08:38.960 --> 08:39.730
GLOWING PIERCE
Glowing Pierce!

08:39.730 --> 08:41.130
GLOWING PIERCE

08:43.630 --> 08:45.460
All right! It worked!

08:45.460 --> 08:47.170
I landed a hit!

08:48.090 --> 08:50.680
Those open spots really
were your weak spots!

08:56.470 --> 08:58.310
Whoa, what's the matter?

08:58.310 --> 09:00.020
Looking to run already?

09:08.490 --> 09:10.570
Are you kidding me?

09:10.570 --> 09:12.990
It's even got some
kinda regenerative ability?

09:14.160 --> 09:17.620
This guy's far from just
"specialized for combat."

09:17.620 --> 09:19.570
It's absolutely flawless!

09:20.040 --> 09:23.000
It's like I'm fighting a Colossus!

09:25.460 --> 09:27.970
What am I scared for?

09:27.970 --> 09:32.890
I'm playing this god-tier game,
this SLF, so I can beat Lycagon!

09:36.220 --> 09:39.230
You're just some Rare Enemy,
not even a Unique!

09:40.100 --> 09:42.480
Ain't no way I will be losing to you!

09:42.480 --> 09:43.730
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
Ain't no way I will be losing to you!

09:43.730 --> 09:44.980
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

09:45.980 --> 09:48.730
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

09:56.910 --> 09:59.660
Your stinger is mine this time!

09:59.660 --> 10:01.830
Glowing Pierce!

10:05.000 --> 10:06.540
What a strength!

10:07.210 --> 10:10.300
I know it's a rare enemy,
but who the heck designed this?!

10:11.170 --> 10:13.680
The devs gotta be rotten to the core!

10:14.310 --> 10:16.220
Even if I weave my way
through its onslaught

10:16.220 --> 10:19.930
and persistently aim
for its open points to damage it,

10:19.930 --> 10:23.520
it will make a distance from me
and heal the damage away.

10:24.600 --> 10:26.520
I can't say for sure,

10:26.520 --> 10:30.450
but it seems to regenerate by spreading
its claws under the moonlight.

10:31.610 --> 10:33.320
Come to think of it...

10:33.900 --> 10:37.530
The moon also had something to do
with meeting Setsuna the Bygone Days.

10:38.450 --> 10:41.540
Is it absorbing the magical energy
of the moon to recover itself?

10:42.290 --> 10:44.960
Is there something special
about the moon in SLF?

10:46.880 --> 10:49.920
Anyway, I gotta find a way
to stop it from healing!

10:52.670 --> 10:54.380
Glowing Pierce!

10:56.300 --> 10:56.690
ENDURANCE LOW

10:56.690 --> 10:57.180
WARNING: BREAKAGE
CHANGE WEAPON

10:57.180 --> 11:00.100
Damn it! It can't take it much longer!

11:03.180 --> 11:07.690
In the end, my Empire Bee Twinblades'
Corrosive Poison got healed and meant nothing.

11:08.610 --> 11:12.990
I only have two transport worth of MP left.

11:13.370 --> 11:17.990
I haven't had a battle this intense since
the one with Wethermon the Tombguard.

11:18.360 --> 11:19.660
Interesting!

11:20.550 --> 11:22.910
I'll use everything I have on you!

11:23.410 --> 11:25.080
Vorpal Blade Tech!

11:25.080 --> 11:26.920
Mirror Reflection!

11:27.170 --> 11:29.040
VORPAL BLADE TECH
MIRROR REFLECTION

11:32.300 --> 11:35.550
Basically, I just have to make sure
you don't have the time to recover!

11:35.550 --> 11:36.340
Skill...

11:36.340 --> 11:37.050
BOUNDLESS MASSACRE

11:37.050 --> 11:38.840
BOUNDLESS MASSACRE
Boundless Massacre!

11:42.180 --> 11:44.480
It's a powerful attack skill
that lets me continuously

11:44.480 --> 11:46.270
slash my enemies until
my stamina runs out.

11:46.270 --> 11:47.770
It deals a lot of damage,

11:47.770 --> 11:51.190
but all this swinging makes
it hard for me to dodge!

11:53.280 --> 11:56.150
But I have this!

11:56.150 --> 11:57.490
Enter Travel!

12:00.740 --> 12:04.410
I can't just use it infinitely,
but this is a good start!

12:04.410 --> 12:06.250
I'm far from over!

12:15.260 --> 12:17.300
Healing again?!

12:17.300 --> 12:17.970
That damn prick!

12:17.970 --> 12:18.630
WEAPON UNEQUIPPED
That damn prick!

12:18.630 --> 12:19.130
MARSH DAGGERS [V3]
EQUIPPED

12:19.760 --> 12:21.890
Not on my watch!

12:25.520 --> 12:26.390
Seven-Boat Leap!

12:26.390 --> 12:27.520
SEVEN-BOAT LEAP
Seven-Boat Leap!

12:27.520 --> 12:28.100
SEVEN-BOAT LEAP

12:29.520 --> 12:32.520
Think you can keep healing
without a care in the world?!

12:32.940 --> 12:35.480
Hand of Fortune!

12:35.480 --> 12:37.740
HAND OF FORTUNE

12:44.080 --> 12:45.790
C'mon, what's wrong?!

12:45.790 --> 12:48.080
You haven't fixed yourself up yet!

12:54.040 --> 12:59.010
Looks like you can't bask in the moonlight
without holding both your claws up.

12:59.550 --> 13:00.970
This is getting fun!

13:00.970 --> 13:02.090
MOONBLADE
MAX - FUSION READY

13:02.490 --> 13:05.140
My Moonblade's Fusion
gauge has been filled!

13:09.480 --> 13:12.100
MOONDBLADE: TWINMOON
Moondblade: Twinmoon!

13:13.980 --> 13:16.110
Time to warp this up!

13:19.360 --> 13:19.950
CLEAVER

13:19.950 --> 13:22.110
CLEAVER
Cleaver!

13:26.370 --> 13:31.620
Just let me cut it off already!

13:35.790 --> 13:37.190
All right!

13:37.190 --> 13:39.340
I finally cleaved that thing right off!

13:42.300 --> 13:43.180
Heh!

13:43.620 --> 13:45.970
I'm not the same guy as the last time.

13:47.930 --> 13:49.350
Sky Walker!

13:53.850 --> 13:57.360
I got the rare part of a rare enemy!

13:57.690 --> 14:00.860
Gotta shove it into
the Invetoria right away.

14:13.250 --> 14:16.670
Heh, getting all riled up after
losing your precious stinger?

14:23.980 --> 14:27.430
Whoa, whoa.
Don't make this harder for me.

14:28.060 --> 14:30.940
I can only teleport one more time.

14:32.310 --> 14:33.810
Hang on...

14:34.330 --> 14:36.310
I got it!

14:37.190 --> 14:39.360
I can finally see it, golden scorpion!

14:39.360 --> 14:42.280
My way to take you down!

14:45.240 --> 14:47.240
Skate Foot!

14:48.740 --> 14:49.240
Heh!

14:51.100 --> 14:54.290
C'mon, follow me, ya dumb scorpions!

14:56.250 --> 15:00.010
Don't worry! I won't dump you all
in a canyon or anythin'!

15:01.710 --> 15:05.130
How long are all
the other guys gonna sleep?!

15:05.970 --> 15:07.010
Wake up!

15:07.010 --> 15:09.260
Crystal Scorpions!

15:14.600 --> 15:19.900
When I first met the golden scorpion,
it was attacking the Crystal Scorpions.

15:19.900 --> 15:21.820
That means they're enemies.

15:21.820 --> 15:24.990
So if I can get the two sides
in the same space,

15:24.990 --> 15:27.360
I won't have to fight them personally!

15:27.750 --> 15:29.700
All right, this should do it!

15:32.620 --> 15:33.580
Too slow!

15:36.080 --> 15:37.580
Seven-Boat Leap!

15:42.920 --> 15:45.920
You shouldn't solely focus on me, y'know?

15:46.360 --> 15:51.310
The guys who can crush you
are coming at you in a pack.

15:51.310 --> 15:53.060
Good luck!

15:53.060 --> 15:54.560
Enter Travel!

15:59.230 --> 16:02.440
I know well enough
how insanely strong you are.

16:03.400 --> 16:09.240
But to fight against that many
Crystal Scorpions without your vision...

16:09.750 --> 16:12.740
I doubt not even you
could handle all of them.

16:14.120 --> 16:16.580
It's over, golden scorpion.

16:16.580 --> 16:18.540
You lost.

16:27.800 --> 16:30.520
Okay, let's head back now.

16:30.520 --> 16:33.390
Even if there are still
some Crystal Scorpions left,

16:33.390 --> 16:35.810
I can just drop 'em off a cliff again.

16:36.770 --> 16:38.310
Exit Travel!

16:52.320 --> 16:56.830
Yay! The golden scorpion is down!

16:57.750 --> 16:59.540
Don't blame me for this!

16:59.540 --> 17:01.210
All is fair in love and...

17:05.630 --> 17:06.630
Whoa!

17:09.130 --> 17:10.720
This guy...

17:20.730 --> 17:23.050
Did it defeat them all?

17:23.050 --> 17:25.730
All of those Crystal Scorpions?

17:27.730 --> 17:30.480
Sorry, man.
I underestimated you.

17:31.740 --> 17:35.740
If anyone's gonna be the one
to kill you, it's gotta be me!

17:41.290 --> 17:44.210
I don't have enough MP to
use Enter Travel anymore,

17:44.210 --> 17:45.790
but I can still win this!

17:51.590 --> 17:56.010
Without its eyes, is it using vibrations
to speculate my location?

17:56.010 --> 17:59.270
It's not attacking
as sharply as it did before.

17:59.930 --> 18:01.440
But...

18:02.840 --> 18:04.810
It's pushing me away!

18:08.190 --> 18:13.280
The magic shooting out of him like steam
is keeping me from moving around well!

18:13.700 --> 18:15.450
In that case...

18:15.450 --> 18:16.200
Go!

18:16.780 --> 18:18.200
Blast Soil Idol!

18:32.470 --> 18:37.180
"When the idol's dance
reaches its climax,

18:37.180 --> 18:39.220
flames will erupt within the ground."

18:53.570 --> 18:57.570
That claw's putting you off balance.

18:58.160 --> 19:00.580
I will cut them for you.

19:04.250 --> 19:06.080
Vorpal Blade Tech...

19:10.920 --> 19:11.510
VORPAL BLADE TECH: HALF-MOON SLASH

19:11.510 --> 19:13.510
VORPAL BLADE TECH: HALF-MOON SLASH
Half-Moon Slash!

19:13.510 --> 19:14.470
VORPAL BLADE TECH: HALF-MOON SLASH

19:19.890 --> 19:22.470
Now you have no weapons left.

19:27.080 --> 19:28.770
The sun is rising.

19:28.770 --> 19:30.650
Time for you to go down like the moon.

19:35.780 --> 19:39.280
It can still move its tail?!

19:39.910 --> 19:41.010
Damn it.

19:41.010 --> 19:44.290
My Empire Bee Twinblades are
only a few hits away from breaking.

19:44.680 --> 19:46.540
I can't strike the final blow.

19:47.580 --> 19:50.040
I'm the one without his weapon...

19:50.040 --> 19:51.380
What now?!

19:52.050 --> 19:53.300
SKY WALKER

19:53.300 --> 19:54.090
No.

19:56.800 --> 19:58.300
I do have one!

19:58.300 --> 20:00.550
A completely fine pair of daggers!

20:02.970 --> 20:06.980
Looking back, we've known
each other for a while now.

20:06.980 --> 20:09.980
Time to settle this! Marsh Dagger!

20:09.980 --> 20:12.820
Glowing Pierce!

20:19.320 --> 20:21.160
Golden scorpion.

20:22.490 --> 20:25.870
I would never have beaten you
without my Inventoria.

20:42.140 --> 20:45.100
You were a formidable foe
on par with Wethermon.

20:55.930 --> 20:58.320
That was super fun.

20:59.280 --> 21:02.990
Shangri-La Frontier is the best game ever!

22:39.630 --> 22:43.300
SLF Theater!

22:43.300 --> 22:44.680
#33: EMUL'S DAY
Mini!

22:44.680 --> 22:46.220
#33: EMUL'S DAY

22:49.150 --> 22:52.810
I wonder what Emul is doing
while I'm away.

22:53.730 --> 22:58.230
LOGGED OUT

22:58.660 --> 23:01.110
Mr. Sunraku is resting.

23:01.110 --> 23:03.000
He's sleeping soundly.

23:03.780 --> 23:05.740
As for me...

23:08.240 --> 23:12.370
Cleaning! Cleaning!

23:12.370 --> 23:16.330
I'm putting a blanket on his tummy
to keep the cold away.

23:17.540 --> 23:20.460
I'll clean your face.

23:20.460 --> 23:23.550
LOGGED OUT
I'll sing you a lullaby.

23:23.550 --> 23:28.180
LOGGED OUT
Sleep, sleep, roll~

23:28.180 --> 23:31.560
LOGGED OUT
Oh you roll~

23:32.010 --> 23:36.520
Mr. Sunraku is a good boy~!

23:36.520 --> 23:40.360
So go to sleep~

23:40.360 --> 23:41.520
Are you a young mom?

23:42.280 --> 23:46.280
IN ACTUALITY, THE PLAYER'S AVATAR
WILL DISAPPEAR WHEN THEY'RE LOGGED OUT
